cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SYMBORG: A Cognitive Front-End Layer for Human-AI Interaction"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Akman
    given-names: Cihangir
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pharmacist65/symborg"
abstract: >-
  SYMBORG is a research and design project on the interface contract between
  AI retrieval systems and human attention. It maps the human signal-to-response
  loop, identifies where a non-invasive device can realistically intervene, and
  prototypes a cognitive packet engine that compresses retrieved context into
  brief, timed, agency-preserving cues — with assistive communication for people
  who cannot speak as its primary application.
keywords:
  - human-computer interaction
  - augmentative and alternative communication
  - assistive technology
  - attention
  - cognitive load
  - brain-computer interface
  - accessibility
license: Apache-2.0
